  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "There are <math><msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></math> ways of selecting the rings to be worn.<br />If <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> are the number of the rings on the fingers, we need to find the non-negative integers such that <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;<br />The numbers of such quadruples is <math><msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>=</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>.<br />For each set of <math><mn>5</mn></math> rings, there are <math><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo></math> arrangements.<br />So, the total number of required arrangements is <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>×</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>141120</mn></math>",
    "image": null
  },
